"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe motive for the murder and the culprit were shocking in this work.  \nA psychopathic tendency to commit murder for pleasure and control is shown.  \nIt even appears to be behavior consistent with what is defined as a  today, in the way all these crimes are organized like a diary in a notebook.  \n\nMany characters in the work also had a guess about the culprit but were depicted as trying to ignore or deny it.  \nReaders who noticed quickly might have felt a bit frustrated by this appearance.  \n\nThe action of one character who learned the truth at the end remains strongly in my impression.\n"